      },
      "lineNbr": 1090,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-11T00:46:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This will potentially disrupt the PE state. We should set a flag instead.\n\nThat being said, I\u0027m not sure we need to do this at all. Nothing is waiting for the Exit Mode process to finish, so it doesn\u0027t need to happen as fast as possible. If the port partner is still attached, we\u0027ll make it back to a ready state pretty soon anyway. I think the TC could call directly into the DPM, and this function could go away.",
      "revId": "4c819d34a029d92dc0d6a3729ac4a3ba3de70bb4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bc8968a7_7c7c171c",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-11T00:46:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the long term, this will probably go away when the DPM becomes its own task or at least state machine to interact with host commands. In the medium term, this should probably be a single entry point into the DPM for the DPM to decide what to do.\n\nFor this CL, can you switch the order of these? If we\u0027ve already decided to exit, it seems pointless to finish the entry sequence first.",
